# Copy to .env.local and fill in. `npm run setup` does it for you.

# Encrypts each learner's own Anthropic key (AES-256-GCM, src/lib/secrets.ts).
# Generated by `npm run setup`. KEEP IT: changing it loses nobody's progress
# but makes every stored API key unreadable, and everyone has to paste theirs
# again. Without it the app refuses to store a key at all, rather than writing
# somebody else's live credential into the database in the clear.
DEUTSCHMATE_SECRET=

# The address this install is reachable at. Defaults to http://localhost:3000.
# Only used for display now — sign-in is a username and a password, so nothing
# is sent anywhere and there is no link to point at the wrong host.
DEUTSCHMATE_URL=

# Nothing to configure for sign-in. There is no email: an account is a username,
# a password and a recovery code shown once. `npm run passwd <username>` is the
# operator's reset when somebody loses both.

# OPTIONAL, and mostly for a single-person install.
#
# Each learner brings their own key in Einstellungen; this one is only a
# fallback for accounts that have not. On a shared or public deployment, leave
# it empty — then nobody's usage lands on your bill.
#
# Everything except four things works WITHOUT any key, and each of the four
# fails honestly rather than silently:
#   conversation -> the unit's scripted branching dialogue
#   writing      -> queued locally, corrected whenever a key/network appears
#   "Erklär mir das" -> served from cache if anyone has asked before;
#                       otherwise it says it is unavailable
# Wrong answers are still explained: the rule-based tier needs no key.
# That is by design (spec §17): a session must be finishable offline.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# The DEFAULT ceiling, in dollars per learner per rolling 30 days. Each learner
# can set their own in Einstellungen, and it is their money now, so this is only
# the starting point.
#
# ENFORCED, not just displayed: every paid call checks the month's spend first
# and falls back to the offline path once it is gone — the same path a missing
# key takes, so a session is still finishable. 0 means no AI spending at all.
DEUTSCHMATE_BUDGET=5

# Lets a request name a learner other than the one in the cookie, via ?user= or
# a "user" field in a POST body. THE TEST SUITE IS THE ONLY THING THAT NEEDS IT:
# six suites drive throwaway learners, and isolation by user id is exactly the
# mechanism they should be exercising.
#
# Without it, both are ignored entirely and every request is whoever the cookie
# says — which is what you want anywhere other people can reach the server.
# `npm run setup` generates one; delete the line to turn impersonation off.
# Fails closed: no variable, no trust. Must be at least 24 characters.
DEUTSCHMATE_TEST_AUTH=

# The admin tools at /admin write to SHARED content — /api/video runs
# `UPDATE unit SET video_id`, which changes the curriculum for every learner.
# Off unless this is exactly "1". A switch, not a password: it stops the
# accidental and the drive-by, and is no defence against someone who can
# already set your environment.
DEUTSCHMATE_ADMIN=

# Wikimedia requires a User-Agent naming your tool AND a contact URL.
# Without one you get 403 "Please honor our robot policy" — an example.com
# email is rejected too. Only needed when running `npm run audio`.
WIKIMEDIA_CONTACT=https://github.com/yourname/deutschmate; your@email.com
